From 2ee12177465b278f1ce540ae634e101163f4cb56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:41:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(desktop): sync timeline rail, Simple-mode rail, square
 menu and launch precedence

- desktop.md said hovering the timeline rail pops open the list of
  prompts and that the rail appears once a chat has a handful of turns.
  TimelineRail (apps/desktop/src/components/assistant-ui/thread/
  timeline-rail.tsx) wraps each marker in its own tooltip, and
  ActiveThreadTimeline renders whenever there is at least one prompt.
- desktop.md said Simple mode keeps the profile rail with more than one
  profile. SIMPLE policy in apps/desktop/src/store/interface-mode.ts keeps
  it when profileCount > 1 || connectionCount > 1.
- multi-connection-desktop.md listed the at-rest square menu without
  Open in new window / Set as default. RestSquare prepends
  ProfileLaunchMenuSection (profile-launch-menu.tsx), which shows
  Open in new window when the shell supports it and Set as default.
- desktop.md described an "Open on launch" control with Primary gateway /
  Last used options; the only control is the "At startup, return to
  Sessions on the last-used gateway" toggle (connections-registry.tsx).
  Neither page said that a default profile wins: the startup selection in
  apps/desktop/src/store/connections.ts follows $defaultProfileRoute before
  looking at launchMode, and electron/main.ts connects that route at
  startup.

Docs only; no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
